From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Find gdesktop-enums.h through includedir, not prefix

Two panels feed gsettings-desktop-schemas' enum header to
gnome.mkenums_simple() and locate it by asking pkg-config for prefix and
appending the rest of the path by hand:

    gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'prefix')
        + '/include/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'

Under a sysroot that is the wrong variable. A cross pkg-config prefixes
includedir and libdir with the sysroot but leaves prefix alone - prefix
is /usr on the target and means nothing on the build machine - so the
constructed path lands in the build machine's /usr/include, and files()
rejects it:

    panels/background/meson.build:25:24: ERROR: File
    /usr/include/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h does not
    exist.

Ask for includedir instead, which is both what is meant and what the
sysroot machinery handles. gsettings-desktop-schemas exports it as of
the patch carried alongside this one.

--- a/panels/background/meson.build
+++ b/panels/background/meson.build
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 )
 
 gdesktop_enums_header = files(
-  gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'prefix') + '/include/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'
+  gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'includedir') + '/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'
 )
 
 common_sources += gnome.mkenums_simple(
--- a/panels/system/meson.build
+++ b/panels/system/meson.build
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@
 )
 
 gdesktop_enums_header = files(
-  gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'prefix') + '/include/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'
+  gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'includedir') + '/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'
 )
 
 sources += gnome.mkenums_simple(
